\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I to the hills will lift mine eyes,
\par From whence doth come mine aid;
\par My safety cometh from the Lord,
\par Who heaven and earth hath made.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thy foot He will not let slide, nor will
\par He slumber that thee keeps;
\par Behold, He that keeps Israel,
\par He slumbers not, nor sleeps.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The Lord thee keeps, the Lord thy shade
\par On thy right hand doth stay;
\par The moon by night thee shall not smite,
\par Nor yet the sun by day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The Lord shall keep thy soul; He shall
\par Preserve thee from all ill;
\par Henceforth thy going out and in
\par God keep for ever will.  
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

